Work in the current working directory and complete this goal:

Act as a principal product designer specializing in macOS menu-bar utilities. Design best-in-class onboarding and steady-state UX for an MSW monitor that must do all installation and GitHub setup in-app, then remain unobtrusive in the status bar. Cover first run, GitHub OAuth/device flow, workspace selection/repository access, progress and failure recovery, compact popover hierarchy, detail window, settings, notifications, destructive confirmations, quick actions, offline/stale data, and macOS 26 visual language. Map every user need to an intuitive surface and say what must never be hidden behind a generic menu. Ground the proposal in the repository command set and Apple conventions. Do not edit files, run project-wide tests, formatters, or linters.

Keep the change minimal and focused. Verify the work. Report a concise summary and every file changed.


**REQUIRED OUTPUT** — You MUST return ONLY a raw JSON object matching this schema:
{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "summary": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 20
    },
    "filesChanged": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "string"
      }
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "summary",
    "filesChanged"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
Do not include prose, markdown, headings, commentary, or code fences.
The first character of your response must be `{` and the last character must be `}`.
The workflow will fail unless the entire response is the JSON object.

